  "problem": "Channel additivity violations",
  "collection": "Original research investigation",
  "summary": "A consequence derived only inside a contradiction branch was stated as an unconditional strict bound on a subset of the slacks.",
  "review_status": "source_reviewed",
  "review_note": "No open interpretation blocker was recorded in the preceding source review. This is not a new independent mathematical verification.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "with the fifth centered pair \\(\\{\\pm m_r\\}\\) arbitrary and all twelve slopes distinct, the independently regenerated determinant census gives\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\n\\Delta_{\\rm ray}+\\Delta_{\\rm flat}>3318E.\n}\n$$\n\n[...]\n\n$$\n\\Delta_{\\rm ray}\n+\\Delta_{\\rm flat}\n+\\Delta_{\\rm Young}\n+\\Delta_{\\rm group}<HE.\n\\tag{1.3}\n$$\n\nThen, individually,\n\n$$\n\\Delta_{\\rm ray}<HE,\\qquad\n\\Delta_{\\rm flat}<HE.\n\\tag{1.4}\n$$",
    "context": "The proof introduces four nonnegative slacks: ray, flat, Young, and group. Its detailed argument assumes their total is less than H E as a contradiction hypothesis, with H=3318 in this case.",
    "locator": "round-59-response.md, lines 14–20, 118–132"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "A consequence derived only inside a contradiction branch was stated as an unconditional strict bound on a subset of the slacks.",
    "evidence": "Let T=Delta_ray+Delta_flat+Delta_Young+Delta_group. The argument derives (T<HE) => (Delta_ray+Delta_flat>HE), contradicting T<HE because all slacks are nonnegative. The valid unconditional conclusion is T>=HE, not Delta_ray+Delta_flat>HE. For a logical counterassignment, E=H=1, Delta_ray=Delta_flat=0, Delta_Young=1, Delta_group=0 makes T>=HE true and the claimed subsidiary bound false, while the contradiction implication holds vacuously.",
    "scope": "argument_invalid"
  },
